WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.734
Morb was still in the dungeon, waiting for the trolls to arrive with the leeches.

2
00:00:05.735 --> 00:00:13.103
"So, Morb," Boz taunted, clutching the bars of his cell, "what happened to your prisoners at the zoo?

3
00:00:13.104 --> 00:00:19.146
My friend Teplo told me they all escaped. Now how could that have happened?"

4
00:00:19.147 --> 00:00:24.057
In the next cell, Teplo smirked. "Well, Boz, let me tell you.

5
00:00:24.058 --> 00:00:29.268
Apparently Morb's trolls were tricked by a pile of turnips."

6
00:00:29.269 --> 00:00:33.062
"Turnips, you say?" Boz laughed.

7
00:00:33.063 --> 00:00:40.544
"That is correct," said Teplo. "Perhaps Morb's not as powerful as he thinks he is, huh?"

8
00:00:40.545 --> 00:00:50.413
Morb ignored the old men, his gaze moving past them to a couple huddled together in a cell farther down the corridor. He walked toward them.

9
00:00:50.414 --> 00:00:58.835
"Hello, Mother and Father," he greeted them with a twisted smile. "I hope the accommodations suit you."

10
00:00:58.836 --> 00:01:01.568
His mother looked up with tears in her eyes.

11
00:01:01.569 --> 00:01:05.143
"Why are you doing this, Morb?" she whispered.

12
00:01:05.144 --> 00:01:12.989
"Don't let him get to you, Mother!" a handsome young Red called from a few cells down. "He never did appreciate you."

13
00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:19.693
"True, I didn't appreciate being ignored and misunderstood," Morb snapped, glaring at his brother.

14
00:01:19.694 --> 00:01:22.413
Meanwhile his father climbed to his feet.

15
00:01:22.414 --> 00:01:26.671
"Son, please think about what you're doing," he said.

16
00:01:26.672 --> 00:01:29.858
"Didn't we teach you right from wrong?"

17
00:01:29.859 --> 00:01:39.888
Morb turned away from him. "You taught me that I'd better do whatever was necessary to take care of myself. And I learned that lesson well."

18
00:01:39.889 --> 00:01:47.923
"Nobody had to teach you to be selfish, Morb!" a young woman—one of his sisters—called from nearby. "You were born that way!" Morb

19
00:01:47.924 --> 00:01:55.147
ignored her too. He'd just heard heavy footsteps coming down the stairs. Good. The trolls were here. "Bring

20
00:01:55.148 --> 00:02:01.663
the cauldron to me," he called to them, not looking at his parents as his mother started to sob. "We'll

21
00:02:01.664 --> 00:02:07.020
start right here, in this cell." "I

22
00:02:07.021 --> 00:02:11.333
wish I had a map," Zann muttered, peeking around a corner. "I've

23
00:02:11.334 --> 00:02:13.907
got to get back to my friends." Zann

24
00:02:13.908 --> 00:02:18.731
had been walking through the palace for some time and had not yet found an exit. All

25
00:02:18.732 --> 00:02:23.482
he'd found were winding stairways and dark, narrow corridors. The

26
00:02:23.483 --> 00:02:26.683
palace was much bigger than he'd realized. Creeping

27
00:02:26.684 --> 00:02:32.434
down another flight of steps, Zann diligently watched for any trolls that might be around. He

28
00:02:32.435 --> 00:02:35.261
thought briefly about just zapping out. After

29
00:02:35.262 --> 00:02:39.366
all, that Deceleration spell hadn't attracted Morb's attention. But

30
00:02:39.367 --> 00:02:43.440
it probably wasn't worth the risk. There had to be a way out somewhere. "Aha!"

31
00:02:43.441 --> 00:02:50.634
Zann whispered when he saw sunlight pouring in through a large doorway at the end of a long hallway. He

32
00:02:50.635 --> 00:02:58.516
hurried forward. But the doorway was not an exit—it led to a balcony overlooking the huge courtyard at the center of the palace. "What

33
00:02:58.517 --> 00:03:06.672
in the world is that ?" Zann blurted out in surprise when he saw the huge, dark, hulking shape in the middle of the courtyard.

34
00:03:06.673 --> 00:03:10.335
Zann immediately thought about what Gliss had told them yesterday.

35
00:03:10.336 --> 00:03:16.786
Could this be the horrible magic-sucking machine that Morb had built to help him take over Magica?

36
00:03:16.787 --> 00:03:21.886
He was still staring at the machine when he heard voices approaching. One of them belonged to Slib.

37
00:03:21.887 --> 00:03:25.886
"Uh-oh," Zann whispered. There was nowhere to hide on the balcony.

38
00:03:25.887 --> 00:03:30.530
Looking around, Zann saw some pebbles in a planter. They gave him an idea.

39
00:03:30.531 --> 00:03:35.194
He picked up one of the pebbles and threw it down the hall, past Slib and the others.

40
00:03:35.195 --> 00:03:38.174
It hit a wall and made a sound. Click

41
00:03:38.175 --> 00:03:45.476
! "What was that?" said Slib. Everyone turned around, and Zann quickly dashed into a room across the

42
00:03:45.477 --> 00:03:51.291
hall. "I'm sure it's nothing," said someone else, as the group continued walking closer to

43
00:03:51.292 --> 00:03:56.480
Zann. Zann held his breath—he could hear Slib and the others right outside the

44
00:03:56.481 --> 00:04:04.457
door. "You can believe what I say since I'm now Morb's most trusted adviser," Slib was

45
00:04:04.458 --> 00:04:08.891
bragging. "The era of Reds is truly over, just as I

46
00:04:08.892 --> 00:04:15.125
predicted. Thanks to King Morb, the rest of us will now have the power we

47
00:04:15.126 --> 00:04:19.431
deserve." One of his companions murmured something in response, but Zann wasn't

48
00:04:19.432 --> 00:04:25.049
listening. He barely had time to dash through another doorway before Slib and the others came into the

49
00:04:25.050 --> 00:04:29.275
room. Zann found himself in a hallway lined with half a dozen

50
00:04:29.276 --> 00:04:33.060
doors. Behind him, he could hear Slib still bragging loudly.

51
00:04:33.061 --> 00:04:35.076
Zann reached for the first door.

52
00:04:35.077 --> 00:04:38.921
"Ouch!" he blurted out, as the doorknob burned his hand.

53
00:04:38.922 --> 00:04:46.353
"Did you hear that?" Slib's muffled voice came from the other room. "There's someone behind that door."

54
00:04:46.354 --> 00:04:49.034
Zann gulped. He had to get out of sight!

55
00:04:49.035 --> 00:04:54.533
But when he looked down the hall, all the doorknobs were glowing red, just like the one he'd touched.

56
00:04:54.534 --> 00:05:00.240
No—not all of them. He spotted one doorknob that was glowing blue.

57
00:05:00.241 --> 00:05:02.860
He hurried toward it, but then he hesitated.

58
00:05:02.861 --> 00:05:05.955
Who had put a spell on these doors, and why?

59
00:05:05.956 --> 00:05:08.488
He'd never seen this kind of spell before.

60
00:05:08.489 --> 00:05:13.819
Normally people just used an ordinary Shield spell if they wanted to keep others out of a room.

61
00:05:13.820 --> 00:05:16.866
Then he heard the door behind him start to open.

62
00:05:16.867 --> 00:05:20.524
If he didn't get out of this hallway, Slib would see him!

63
00:05:20.525 --> 00:05:25.051
Grabbing the blue doorknob, he was relieved to find it cool under his hand.

64
00:05:25.052 --> 00:05:28.828
He pushed through the door, allowing it to fall shut behind him.

65
00:05:28.829 --> 00:05:33.510
He found himself in what appeared to be a dusty old storage room.

66
00:05:33.511 --> 00:05:36.862
The only light came through a single barred window.

67
00:05:36.863 --> 00:05:42.861
Boxes and crates were piled everywhere, and a couple of dust bugs scuttled off behind a trunk.

68
00:05:42.862 --> 00:05:47.408
Zann heard a sound behind him. Spinning around, he gasped.

69
00:05:47.409 --> 00:05:57.531
Standing in a dim corner of the room was the old woman he and his friends had met in Wormwood.

